# Overview

As a software engineer, my goal is to create robust applications that enhance user experience and facilitate better management of personal finances.
 Through this project, I developed a Personal Budget Management Application using C#, which allows users to track their income, expenses, and savings
  effectively. This software demonstrates my understanding of object-oriented programming principles, data persistence, and user interface design,
   enabling me to further my learning in C#.

The purpose of writing this software was to deepen my understanding of C# language syntax and features, including file handling, exception handling,
 and class structures. This hands-on experience has strengthened my programming skills and provided me with insights into building functional 
 applications that meet user needs.



[Software Demo Video](http://youtube.link.goes.here)

# Development Environment

To develop this software, I utilized Visual Studio, a powerful IDE for C# development, which provided essential tools for code editing, debugging, 
and project management. The programming language used is C#, taking advantage of its object-oriented capabilities to structure the application 
effectively.

I also incorporated Newtonsoft.Json library for JSON file handling, allowing for easy serialization and deserialization of financial data, which 
supports data persistence in the application.



